 $y=12\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)$ at the point $(1+\\pi ,-12).$\n\n{{selection}}" 13194139535290 17592186045443 true] [17592186491422 1072 #uuid "a8a0d3c1-7c1b-5f34-8315-2483a617ccdf" 13194139535290 17592186045443 true] [17592186491422 1074 "First, the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=1+\\pi $ is given by ${f}^{′}(1+\\pi ).$\n\nWe will calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ using the chain rule. First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=12\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,u=x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=1+\\pi ,$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(1+\\pi ) & =-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1+\\pi -1) \\\\  & =-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at the point $(1+\\pi ,-12):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-12) & =0(x-(1+\\pi )) \\\\ y+12 & =0 \\\\ y & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535290 17592186045443 true] [17592186491423 1080 "y=x - 12 - \\pi" 13194139535290 17592186045443 true] [17592186491423 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535290 17592186045443 true] [17592186491423 1083 #uuid "aba5c3d1-b904-56ff-b6f0-a46b86905b0d" 13194139535290 17592186045443 true] [17592186491424 1080 "y=x - 3 + \\pi" 13194139535290 17592186045443 true] [17592186491424 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535290 17592186045443 true] [17592186491424 1083 #uuid "cc514de1-4d5e-554f-a6ba-78fec0fab754" 13194139535290 17592186045443 true] [17592186491425 1068 #edb/ref 17592186491417 13194139535290 17592186045443 true] [17592186491425 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535290 17592186045443 true] [1759218